8. Create a Jenkins project
Now we'll connect your GitHub repository.

Go to Jenkins Dashboard.

Click New Item.

Enter a project name:

GitHub-Tomcat-Deployment
Select Freestyle project.

Click OK.


Step 8.1 – Connect GitHub
Under Source Code Management:

Select Git.

Enter your Git repository URL.

Example:

https://github.com/username/project.git
3. Branch Specifier:

*/main
If your repository uses master, enter */master instead.

If your repository is private, add your GitHub credentials.

